            <svg class="crs-pin-check" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="crs-pin" data-target="m6-checkin-1">
            <div class="crs-pin-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg></div>
            <span class="crs-pin-label">6 Months</span>
            <svg class="crs-pin-check" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="crs-pin" data-target="m6-checkin-2">
            <div class="crs-pin-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 7h8m0 0v8m0-8l-8 8-4-4-6 6"/></svg></div>
            <span class="crs-pin-label">1 Year</span>
            <svg class="crs-pin-check" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="crs-pin-detail is-open" data-detail="m6-checkin-0"><strong>30 Days</strong><p>Check that turnover went smoothly and there are no lingering warranty or move-in concerns. This is where a client decides whether you disappear the moment the commission clears.</p></div>
    <div class="crs-pin-detail" data-detail="m6-checkin-1"><strong>6 Months</strong><p>A light, no-agenda check-in — how's the unit, how's the neighborhood settling in. Keeps you top of mind without asking for anything.</p></div>
    <div class="crs-pin-detail" data-detail="m6-checkin-2"><strong>1 Year</strong><p>Send an updated property value estimate for their unit. This is often the moment a referral happens naturally, since you've just reminded them their purchase was a good decision.</p></div>

    <p>80% of buyers say they would use their agent again, but only 20% actually do — almost always because the agent failed to stay in touch. Your past clients are your most profitable future lead source, but only if you keep the relationship alive. A simple recurring reminder in your CRM for each of these three milestones is usually all it takes to turn this into a habit instead of an intention.</p>
    <div class="crs-scenario">
        <strong>🇵🇭 Philippine Scenario</strong>
        <p>A year after turnover, you send a past client a short message with updated resale values for similar units in their building, congratulating them on the appreciation. They reply thanking you — and two weeks later refer their officemate, who's now looking to buy in the same area.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="crs-takeaway-line"><strong>Core Takeaway:</strong> 80% of buyers say they would use their agent again, but only 20% actually do because the agent failed to stay in touch. Your past clients are your most profitable future lead source.</div>
</article>

<div class="crs-callout">
    <strong>📌 TAKE NOTE — Closing Isn't the Finish Line</strong>
    <p>Treat the handshake at turnover as the start of a relationship, not the end of a transaction. The agents who build a real book of repeat and referral business are the ones who kept showing up long after the commission was paid.</p>
</div>

<div class="crs-key-takeaways">
    <h4>Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Use LAER — Listen, Acknowledge, Explore, Respond — to work through final-hour objections instead of arguing against them.</li>
        <li>Final objections are usually about fear of commitment, not the property — reassure with the data gathered during discovery.</li>
        <li>Act as the conductor during escrow, keeping lenders, title officers, and inspectors on schedule.</li>
        <li>Build a systematic post-close check-in habit — most repeat business is lost to silence, not dissatisfaction.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
